        <item>
         <layout class="QVBoxLayout" name="about_power_line_layout">
          <property name="spacing">
           <number>6</number>
          </property>
          <item>
           <widget class="QLabel" name="about_power_line_title_label">
            <property name="font">
             <font>
              <bold>true</bold>
             </font>
            </property>
            <property name="text">
             <string>About the power line contamination detector</string>
            </property>
           </widget>
          </item>
          <item>
           <widget class="QLabel" name="about_power_line_label">
            <property name="text">
             <string>&lt;b&gt;How the power is computed&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;• The power at the frequency of the power line (60 or 50 Hz) is computed by integrating the power spectral density, estimated with Welch's method [1].&lt;br/&gt;• The power is computed on 6 s windows with a 3 s step.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;(A) Fixed threshold (mean + x SD)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;• The power is log-transformed (log10) to reduce its skewness and bring it closer to a normal distribution.&lt;br/&gt;• Artifacts make the distribution of the power right-skewed. So it is modeled with a three-component Gaussian mixture model (GMM).&lt;br/&gt;• The threshold is the mean of the main Gaussian component plus a multiple of its standard deviation (SD). The main Gaussian component is the one with the largest weight. "(A) Fixed threshold" is the multiple.&lt;br/&gt;• A window is flagged when log10(power at 60 or 50 Hz) &amp;gt; mean + threshold × SD.&lt;br/&gt;• The distribution is computed from all the selected channels of the recording. Excluding a channel with a poor signal changes the threshold of the other channels.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;(B) Power ratio (relative power)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;• A power line contamination can be masked by a strong low-frequency activity. It may then not disturb the EEG.&lt;br/&gt;• A window is flagged when (60 or 50 Hz power) / (1–61 or 1–51 Hz power) &amp;gt; threshold.&lt;br/&gt;• A higher threshold asks for a larger part of the power at the frequency of the power line before a window is an artifact.</string>
            </property>
            <property name="textFormat">
             <enum>Qt::TextFormat::RichText</enum>
            </property>
            <property name="wordWrap">
             <bool>true</bool>
            </property>
            <property name="variant" stdset="0">
             <string notr="true">help</string>
            </property>
           </widget>
          </item>
